123 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 91 0 R
/E (Vermicomposting is the process of using earthworms, primarily red wigglers \(Eisenia fetida\) or African nightcrawlers \(Eudrilus eugeniae\), to convert organic waste into nutrient-rich organic fertilizer \(vermicompost\). This eco-friendly method enhances soil health, promotes regenerative agriculture, and contributes to sustainable waste management systems.)
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
124 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 91 0 R
/E (2. Mzuri Organics Approach to Circularity)
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
125 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 91 0 R
/E (Our model integrates vermicomposting with Black Soldier Fly Larvae \(BSFL\) rearing and greenhouse cultivation. By combining worm castings and BSFL frass, Mzuri Organics produces potent organic biofertilizers. Innovations like Green Tags, embedding tree seeds in frass-infused biodegradable paper, extend our circularity goals to reforestation and soil regeneration.)
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
